  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Frequency",
   "texto": [
    "**Immer** (always), **oft** (often), **manchmal** (sometimes), **nie** (never). They go after the verb.",
    "**Nie** is already negative: it does not carry «nicht». **Ich arbeite nie am Sonntag** (I never work on Sundays).",
    "**Doch** is a special «Yes.»: it is used to carry the opposite to a negative sentence."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Go and do",
   "texto": [
    "**Gehen** (go) and **machen** (do) are regular: **ich gehe, du gehst, er geht**; **ich mache, du machst, er macht**.",
    "**in** + is used to go to a site; with neutral, **in das** is contracted to **ins**: **ins Kino**, **ins Schwimmbad**.",
    "**Mit** = with: **mit Freunden** (with friends)."
   ]
  },
